    "turn_text": "say i think it's totally unnecessary there should have been a path forward here uh... it's very unfortunate that this is being used as a political football uh... and uh... the president is using the wall as a political metaphor in in this case and had reached a deal prior to christmas with the senate i had agreed to a continuing resolution to keep government open that was unanimously passed by the senate and then he went back on his position called the house down to the white house and said i want to resist this Senate proposal back to the Senate, the Republicans voted for it, Senate back to the Senate, and there isn't the votes there to open up government. Worse than that, there was an opportunity back in March and in May to get $25 billion for the wall over uh... or the so-called law and i think the public has to understand that everybody is equally concerned about border security it's how you address the data security in the mall is more of a better for that it is an actual physical thing uh... brand you know representative will hurt these the republican protectors who have the largest amount of border in his district eight hundred twenty miles he's a former cia He called the border wall a fallacy. And this is the important thing. It's not how many miles of oil that is going to keep us safe. It's hardly keeping the bad people like gangs and trucks. It's during the Soviet epidemic out of the country. And the best way to do that is with technology and manpower. So for God's sake, let's get back there and roll up our compromise, provide where needed laws, but get the money to keep out the gangs and the drugs and all of the bad elements that happen on the border, and then provide a path forward for children, and provide a platform for dreamers and immigration, and do it in a comprehensive, logical way, the way you would expect your government to work.",
