    "turn_text": "no question about it. And since 1977, there's been 20 government shutdowns. Most have lasted only about three days or less. They shut down in 2013 and may recall I lasted about 60 days. These end up being, and this infuriates the public as well. These end up usually being political fights to make a point. Meanwhile, there are people, essential workers that have to go to work at our airport in a security, et cetera. It doesn't affect anyone in the military. It doesn't affect Social Security, Medicare, and Medicaid, but still, Federal employees over these Christmas holidays, and can you imagine having to go home and say, well, I have to go to work on it, but we may not get paid now. They'll get back paid, but to go through this inconvenience for politics to me, we should be there working through this ourselves throughout the holidays to make sure that there's a solution.",
